[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73856"] :question/problem "Consider the elliptic paraboloid $z=\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}.$ Which of the following gives its axis of symmetry, written as an intersection of two planes?" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our equation as \n\n$$\nz-0=\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic paraboloid oriented along the $z$-axis that has its vertex at $(-1,2,0).$\n Since it is oriented along the $z$-axis, we conclude that its axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe axis of symmetry should pass through the vertex of the paraboloid. Therefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry can be written as an intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1 \\\\ y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164270/selection/5b6396bbf7e81648e3ff4863d11282b60246d73f838d21b62bd973c90253acb2" :answer/id #uuid "a642dfe6-440b-5fe6-b7cb-450e8b855422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4 \\\\ y=2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164270/selection/bd66411ad0ff5049f4aa61ff7085f56496eb9e539cc74741badb8171c199eed1" :answer/id #uuid "d3897975-fc80-5080-97d1-342bbac83079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-4 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164270/selection/2deab12454cce416e66ac01f270775c73b92ac6b1106d134db5302d1d5165f25" :answer/id #uuid "3a461af0-8f31-5b21-a841-4445fea52f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4 \\\\ z=-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164270/selection/f94433149cffa16d778d37f2255554b112836cda0135620df58d78a607f47cee" :answer/id #uuid "283264f1-4bec-5cfe-862f-16bd5e416058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-4 \\\\ y=-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q