n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $x=3$ and $x=7.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(3,0,0)$ and $(7,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164276/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9078ab1-37a4-5e96-ae12-a83d5cd8804e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection/b17e0c25c069113eda59e56c021eafebe3a2341326cdcbe04854cd3565b0c32a" :answer/id #uuid "96437402-c2d3-59bd-b80a-67d75eced1f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two parallel lines: $y=(z\\pm 3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection/cf79a973a0d6a636e0d6b3abf8838eb4c6b90b860179f7b6a42fc5a6407a5650" :answer/id #uuid "6fa89ba4-33fb-559d-8f49-d803872e363d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola: $z=3(y-1)^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection/535933b78b03e1d368828f719556d9b28a9e13e4b0716edaef527fff708dc2c6" :answer/id #uuid "f501fa73-c112-5741-a991-7f431eb1ebc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola: $z=\\frac{1}{3}(y-1)^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection/150641501dd7e70336753e3c84dfb878ed20d79b375e3be6f7c0dfee99b99d55" :answer/id #uuid "9fe085ad-b76e-526d-8c68-5a460e19d40d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two intersecting lines: $y=\\pm (x-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection/b6912b954a44eff9a65eed7d9a2d1239b83dff0676d2793078d39071973a9cbb" :answer/id #uuid "f7082fe7-94a0-52b1-a6fd-e63919cf2b36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola: ${x}^{2}-3(y-1)^{2}=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a72c180d-db2d-56c9-b1b2-0142961a5cc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35931/selection/535933b78b03e1d368828f719556d9b28a9e13e4b0716edaef527fff708dc2c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-35931/selection/b17e0c25c069113eda59e56c021eafebe3a2341326cdcbe04854cd3565b0c32a" "q-35931/selection/cf79a973a0d6a636e0d6b3abf8838eb4c6b90b860179f7b6a42fc5a6407a5650" "q-35931/selection/535933b78b03e1d368828f719556d9b28a9e13e4b0716edaef527fff708dc2c6" "q-35931/selection/150641501dd7e70336753e3c84dfb878ed20d79b375e3be6f7c0dfee99b99d55" "q-35931/selection/b6912b954a44eff9a65eed7d9a2d1239b83dff0676d2793078d39071973a9cbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35931" :question/id #uuid "facb394a-2e83-5e9d-9e73-9cdb8f17ac06" :question/math-academy-id "q-35931" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic paraboloid $z+1=\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ z+1 & =\\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ z+1 & =1+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{3}(y-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff86a8b-7966-53f7-a7bc-287990fb611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection/17fe07d35b2fb3f4d030d80f2407c69d1cd0c177e6a4c376c5b4b246317df19c" :answer/id #uuid "0aa28d17-31fd-5ce1-9bd6-ab74baa6c5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two intersecting lines: $y=\\pm 3(x+2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection/5c885ecbebe1687eef18496967b9ebc6ba698085c97094b7ab7520f01b69e477" :answer/id #uuid "5b79251a-8204-5b0e-b745-15da44fe53a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola: $z=27(y-1)^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection/7bf4f43c7d175852b57bebb19b94816cc39cc67f3696651ee503cc8b897c168f" :answer/id #uuid "60fced49-57fd-5317-b4d5-2477e9dda21b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola: $(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2}=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection/348e5c362629fee8a0a9ecff4447cb0708ca4dc6ec5132c9c63ba37e5ae74a55" :answer/id #uuid "90e98d94-3f3b-5275-910e-c7f59f99c41b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two parallel lines: $x=3(z\\pm 1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection/102c12f9a56160e483c25a0ffb695aba40c7d93d79313f192a0d0cc24c813eab" :answer/id #uuid "006575c1-166b-588d-a44d-089d061fcce4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola: $z=\\frac{1}{27}(y-1)^{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c50c9d03-bbb6-5c45-b005-5339de96dbde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35577/selection/102c12f9a56160e483c25a0ffb695aba40c7d93d79313f192a0d0cc24c813eab" :answer-field/choices ["q-35577/selection/17fe07d35b2fb3f4d030d80f2407c69d1cd0c177e6a4c376c5b4b246317df19c" "q-35577/selection/5c885ecbebe1687eef18496967b9ebc6ba698085c97094b7ab7520f01b69e477" "q-35577/selection/7bf4f43c7d175852b57bebb19b94816cc39cc67f3696651ee503cc8b897c168f" "q-35577/selection/348e5c362629fee8a0a9ecff4447cb0708ca4dc6ec5132c9c63ba37e5ae74a55" "q-35577/selection/102c12f9a56160e483c25a0ffb695aba40c7d93d79313f192a0d0cc24c813eab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35577" :question/id #uuid "69276016-ba7c-50d9-a595-a7d6a823a97c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35577" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic paraboloid $z=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{27}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{27} \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{27}(y-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff86a8b-7966-53f7-a7bc-287990fb611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection/952c65d3525b53f428134a8466e351432ff36696eaf38052c226fbd88b03b8d5" :answer/id #uuid "3f7874b9-57de-5777-abe3-4b6997bcc4d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection/ed5dbeba82587bb410d81c7957615e3384925e576e766761233090ff83097735" :answer/id #uuid "34106f8e-07d2-5126-a941-07361f990c94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection/772f52281ff01c0519c252f2e2cbc83ebe5ae71eaeb999dca1100556e34b4cf8" :answer/id #uuid "ac9ef105-bd46-59cb-98e4-3a819bbd782c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection/1d708705be678df4ad4cd332dcc8f653a0b02c4827e3588ca8917b08b2a46a25" :answer/id #uuid "116365e0-908f-55e4-863c-a4a8f57e20b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection/4edb9e9b3c14f6ec7dfff0e4bdea85d5556a71c25f5d284631a7a325ba650f60" :answer/id #uuid "6c9e8f16-699a-59c2-803f-80f4b1b46cff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6f92b3-41fb-58d0-b775-905658b2c610" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164282/selection/ed5dbeba82587bb410d81c7957615e3384925e576e766761233090ff83097735" :answer-field/choices ["q-164282/selection/952c65d3525b53f428134a8466e351432ff36696eaf38052c226fbd88b03b8d5" "q-164282/selection/ed5dbeba82587bb410d81c7957615e3384925e576e766761233090ff83097735" "q-164282/selection/772f52281ff01c0519c252f2e2cbc83ebe5ae71eaeb999dca1100556e34b4cf8" "q-164282/selection/1d708705be678df4ad4cd332dcc8f653a0b02c4827e3588ca8917b08b2a46a25" "q-164282/selection/4edb9e9b3c14f6ec7dfff0e4bdea85d5556a71c25f5d284631a7a325ba650f60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164282" :question/id #uuid "1dfc46d0-73fb-5732-9512-b29eeb4abe56" :question/math-academy-id "q-164282" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $4(x-5)^{2}+6(y+4)^{2}=z+8$ and the plane \n$z=4$  onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=4$, we substitute $z=4$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-5)^{2}+6(y+4)^{2}=z+8 \\\\ 4(x-5)^{2}+6(y+4)^{2}=4+8 \\\\ 4(x-5)^{2}+6(y+4)^{2}=12 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164282/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff86a8b-7966-53f7-a7bc-287990fb611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection/623a86592d3176cdd1bf5fb9b7e5c36d0408a40503a32cb930ff0bf69121bc68" :answer/id #uuid "0a5e6097-2617-5ac7-b9c0-becce4d07ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,3)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection/987f2e80d7c1ead65a12907f51ed5af3b6ce9e1b237e86886dc6a7067045b180" :answer/id #uuid "86b8e1cc-02a2-58ec-946f-67e7e62c2897" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-3)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection/34ec1878e3cbe93e8d43d37fdefa7ccacc0f06e76698f6e4ac6484740adad272" :answer/id #uuid "e33243f9-bc62-5ece-9da3-3ee3df191a22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection/a2050946adac6fc2dc61d9c08f9bb5c65b690e883eee22dfff3b7afc6b25a120" :answer/id #uuid "a3396991-c8d6-521c-be6d-6ad591fabd87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,3)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection/7454b2a020f926cb6d381bf4994429c65dad6f116336f0cf3414637adec17be7" :answer/id #uuid "c49d7274-e3cd-54ff-aa55-7373b7cb378e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-3)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ddc0cfa-36b7-5ce9-8c12-6769101aa32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35906/selection/7454b2a020f926cb6d381bf4994429c65dad6f116336f0cf3414637adec17be7" :answer-field/choices ["q-35906/selection/623a86592d3176cdd1bf5fb9b7e5c36d0408a40503a32cb930ff0bf69121bc68" "q-35906/selection/987f2e80d7c1ead65a12907f51ed5af3b6ce9e1b237e86886dc6a7067045b180" "q-35906/selection/34ec1878e3cbe93e8d43d37fdefa7ccacc0f06e76698f6e4ac6484740adad272" "q-35906/selection/a2050946adac6fc2dc61d9c08f9bb5c65b690e883eee22dfff3b7afc6b25a120" "q-35906/selection/7454b2a020f926cb6d381bf4994429c65dad6f116336f0cf3414637adec17be7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35906" :question/id #uuid "2c2420eb-a369-5201-ac95-195a1c7fe310" :question/math-academy-id "q-35906" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic paraboloid $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=z+2$ and the plane \n$y=3$  onto the $xz$-plane is a parabola. What is the vertex of this parabola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $y=3$, we substitute $y=3$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =z+2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{9} & =z+2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-1 & =z+2 \\\\ z+3 & =\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4} \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+1)^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xz$-plane that has its vertex at $(-1,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35906/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff86a8b-7966-53f7-a7bc-287990fb611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35906"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection/c7f52a375822b641143170c455b5dcc07f3ef83c8a194c3e27614c8221d8aba5" :answer/id #uuid "abe19fdc-fb69-5928-8d4e-48a390c910a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-3)$ in the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection/5066f7ffe377cd65d11c40968f6f7178f00647a34cb5847309737231ca3bf16a" :answer/id #uuid "bf23ab8f-9ee7-56a6-a801-dd4c72540802" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,3)$ in the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection/9524dc1bf4ffdcc61c5583bf21f611846af424bdb5671c8373801939ea3b092f" :answer/id #uuid "5a1534d6-a901-5c96-94c5-103da52565a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection/85f003d434577dff0c4918c03049ca15d33a489dbc8bdc227dff5984dc589ce6" :answer/id #uuid "24ecf297-1a11-5eba-a344-6dc1ef68cad0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,-3)$ in the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection/601e356e7ea185b5bf350284b7a32d9d190b5a399faecb8d5883536c363847d3" :answer/id #uuid "9ea09b78-4175-54bb-a762-f055d4a78f25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,3)$ in the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a498074-f8f5-5aed-97eb-0ca401a831f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35930/selection/85f003d434577dff0c4918c03049ca15d33a489dbc8bdc227dff5984dc589ce6" :answer-field/choices ["q-35930/selection/c7f52a375822b641143170c455b5dcc07f3ef83c8a194c3e27614c8221d8aba5" "q-35930/selection/5066f7ffe377cd65d11c40968f6f7178f00647a34cb5847309737231ca3bf16a" "q-35930/selection/9524dc1bf4ffdcc61c5583bf21f611846af424bdb5671c8373801939ea3b092f" "q-35930/selection/85f003d434577dff0c4918c03049ca15d33a489dbc8bdc227dff5984dc589ce6" "q-35930/selection/601e356e7ea185b5bf350284b7a32d9d190b5a399faecb8d5883536c363847d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35930" :question/id #uuid "47157beb-5e76-50cf-b21f-0f4f2d19f147" :question/math-academy-id "q-35930" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2}=z$ and the plane $z=2$  onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. Find the center of this ellipse." :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=2$, we substitute $z=2$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2} & =z \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}+3(y+3)^{2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2/5}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{2/3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse in the $xy$-plane that has its center at $(-2,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff86a8b-7966-53f7-a7bc-287990fb611d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5266"] :question/problem "Find the vertex and the axis of symmetry of the elliptic paraboloid $z= 4x^2 + 8(y + 2)^2.$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of an elliptic paraboloid oriented along the $z$-axis with vertex at a point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ is \n\n$$\nz - z_0 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2}.\n$$\n\nTo find the vertex, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-0 & =4{x}^{2}+8(y+2)^{2} \\\\ z-0 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1/4}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{1/8} \\\\ z-0 & =\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{1/4}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{1/8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic paraboloid oriented along the $z$-axis that has its vertex at $(0,-2,0).$  Since it is oriented along the $z$-axis, we conclude that its axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe axis of symmetry should pass through the vertex of the paraboloid. Therefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry can be written as an intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5269"] :question/problem "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+1=\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{4} - (y-2) ^2.$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}-(y-2)^{2} \\\\ z-(-1) & =\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}-(y-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(1,2,-1).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6087"] :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic paraboloid \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{4} - \\dfrac{(y+5) ^2}{3} = z-1\n$$\n\nand the plane $x=2$  onto the $yz$-plane is a parabola. Find the vertex of this parabola." :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $x=2,$ we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the paraboloid and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =z-1 \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =z-1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =z-1 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3}(y+5)^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $yz$-plane, we get the equation of a parabola that has its vertex at $(-5,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
